by fonto at 2026-08-02T13:35:46Z

Hi,

Not the author but interested in getting this patch integrated in the next version of Symfony :)

> Regarding URLs (and tags), this is already the default behavior when not using facets. Any benefits in doing it via facets

To referr to the protocol reference, : Bluesky has no markup language. Facets are the sole mechanism by which a post declares that a byte range is a link, a mention or a hashtag, and the docs are explicit that producing them is the client's job: _"Clients to Bluesky should produce facets using parsers."_

URLs are readable as-is even if not parsed, however this does not work for tags: with no app.bsky.richtext.facet#tag entry, #symfony is inert text — not clickable, and not attached to the tag feed, hence not appearing when searching for #symfony. I was hit first-hand by this problem after posting automatically a few messages for one of my websites.

This patch therefore creates consistency with the other facets types (mentions and links) and strengthens the quality of the implementation.

